    "globalConstraints": "- Every copy under `frontier/` is file by file \u2014 never `cp -R` of a directory \u2014 so the copy that runs again at every later transition nests nothing and rewrites nothing; the boot reads `frontier/` and writes nothing into it.\n- Neither the kernel nor the engine changes: what the sandbox writes under `frontier/` is exactly what it wrote at BASE.\n- The census is python3 stdlib only, reads nothing but the run directories named on its argv \u2014 no `gh`, no git, no network \u2014 and never raises on a malformed record: a file it cannot read is one stderr line and a count of zero, never a traceback.\n- A guarded exam file is self-contained at its guarded path: a boot sim imports only `./_sandbox_boot_helpers.mjs` and node built-ins, and never imports anything under `fleet/tests/exams/`.",
